statement:
Let $S$ be a set with $2002$ elements, and let $N$ be an integer with
$$0\le N\le2^{2002}.$$
Prove that it is possible to color every subset of $S$ either black or white so that the following conditions hold:

(a) the union of any two white subsets is white;

(b) the union of any two black subsets is black;

(c) there are exactly $N$ white subsets.
